  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated approach toward malaria elimination - Guyana (01-Jan-2026-31-Dec-2028)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guyana, Malaria, Ministry of Health of the Co-operative Republic of Guyana (MOH)This program has the following goals: To reduce malaria cases (50% and 70% by 2028 and 2030, respectively) and malaria-related deaths (80% and 100% by 2028 and 2030, respectively) compared to a 2023 baseline and eliminate P. falciparum cases from regions 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, and 10.. The objectives of this program are: Test all suspected cases and treat 100% of confirmed malaria cases at the level of health facilities and communities.</narrative>
  </description>
